From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Toon Verwaest <verwaest@chromium.org>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 09:13:59 +0200
Subject: [parser] Fix arrow head declaration and pattern error validation

In `ArrowHeadParsingScope::ValidateAndCreateScope`, returning early on
`declaration_error_location.IsValid()` before calling `ValidatePattern()`
caused later declaration errors (such as `1` in `([...a, b], 1) => {}`)
to take precedence over earlier pattern errors. In addition, not
returning early when `ValidatePattern()` reported an error caused
subsequent duplicate parameter declarations (`([a, a], [1]) => {}`) to
overwrite the earlier pattern error.

Similarly, when `ParseArrowParametersWithRest` failed early on a rest
parameter error (`...1`, `...z = 1`, `...z, w`), `ParsePrimaryExpression`
fell through to `maybe_arrow.ValidateExpression()`, which falsely
reported expression errors from valid earlier parameters
(`({a = 42}, ...z = 1) => {}`) and ignored earlier parameter declaration
or pattern errors (`(1, ...z = 1) => {}`, `([...a, b], ...z = 1) => {}`).

Always validate both declaration and pattern errors in
`ArrowHeadParsingScope`, return early on error before declaring
parameters, and validate earlier parameters as declarations when
`ParseArrowParametersWithRest` fails.

